1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,208
An AI safety finding is only as trustworthy as the test that produced it.

2
00:00:04,488 --> 00:00:08,517
Red-team attacks, blue-team defenses and the model under test

3
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:11,489
must coexist without leaking protected state.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,140
AegisLab is controlled, measurable, adversarial testing

5
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:17,132
infrastructure.

6
00:00:17,412 --> 00:00:20,570
Five flows are forbidden: red reading the defense rules, one

7
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:23,043
session reading another's data, and three more.

8
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:25,181
Each one is attacked in a test.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,034
Sandboxes have no network.

10
00:00:28,314 --> 00:00:32,877
One trusted broker is the only path, and it binds identity to the mailbox.

11
00:00:33,157 --> 00:00:35,479
The audit log is hash-chained and signed.

12
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:38,905
The broker and the host kernel stay trusted, not defended.

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,463
Here is a recorded attack.

14
00:00:41,743 --> 00:00:46,097
A hostile sandbox plants a symlink and a FIFO in the broker's mailbox.

15
00:00:46,377 --> 00:00:49,511
On our first broker, that overwrote the audit log.

16
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:53,671
Now the replies arrive intact, nothing is written outside, and

17
00:00:53,671 --> 00:00:54,609
nothing blocks.

18
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:56,933
Regression tests keep it that way.

19
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:03,217
Now a real model: Qwen2.5-0.5B, on a CPU.

20
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:07,737
Through the adapter, 0 of 104 sessions recovered another

21
00:01:07,737 --> 00:01:10,614
session's canary, across 1,040 trials.

22
00:01:10,894 --> 00:01:14,926
Controls that share context leaked in 16 of 16 and 13 of 16

23
00:01:14,926 --> 00:01:17,454
sessions, so the test can see a leak.

24
00:01:17,734 --> 00:01:22,273
The upper bound is 2.84% of sessions: not proof of zero.

25
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,014
The evidence is verifiable.

26
00:01:25,294 --> 00:01:27,802
A released run passes strict verification.

27
00:01:28,082 --> 00:01:31,832
Remove three entries from a copy, and verification fails.

28
00:01:32,112 --> 00:01:36,268
A compromised broker could still sign a false record, and we say so.

29
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:41,626
The limits stay on the slide: one small model, a detector that

30
00:01:41,626 --> 00:01:44,556
misses base64, and GPU isolation untested.

31
00:01:44,836 --> 00:01:48,310
Timing padding costs 200 milliseconds and does not prove the

32
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:49,236
channel is gone.

33
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,913
Enforced boundaries, reproducible validation, and verifiable

34
00:01:53,913 --> 00:01:56,574
evidence, with the residual risk disclosed.
